    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Why Hire a Freelancer Instead of an Agency</h2>
        <p>Not always the right call, so here is the honest version.</p>
        <ul class="mb-4">
          <li><strong>You get the senior person.</strong> The person you talk to is the person writing the code.</li>
          <li><strong>Lower overhead.</strong> No account manager, no project coordinator layer, no office to pay for. That shows up in the rate.</li>
          <li><strong>Faster decisions.</strong> Questions get answered the same day because there is nobody to route them through.</li>
          <li><strong>Where an agency wins.</strong> If you need design, copywriting, brand strategy and development at once, or several people starting immediately, an agency is the better fit.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">How Engagements Usually Work</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Fixed-scope projects.</strong> A migration, a new application, a specific build. Scoped up front with a defined ending.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monthly retainers.</strong> A block of hours with a guaranteed response time, for organizations that need ongoing work rather than one project.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Staff augmentation.</strong> Embedded with your team for a stretch, working the way your team works.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Assessments.</strong> A flat-fee look at a system or a stalled project, with a written recommendation. Often the right first step. See <a href="/services/rescue-recovery">rescue and recovery</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-5">
