        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Working Together, Locally or Not</h2>
        <p>I'm in Minneapolis and I'm in the Central time zone, which matters more than people expect. Overlapping business hours means questions get answered the same day instead of the next morning.</p>
        <p>If you are in the Twin Cities and want to meet in person for a kickoff or a working session, that is easy to arrange. Most of the actual work happens remotely, because that is how software gets built now, but being an hour from your office instead of nine time zones away changes how a project feels.</p>
        <p>I also work with clients well outside Minnesota. Being local is a convenience, not a requirement.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

